WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.267
Welcome back, future creators!

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.567
Before we start building our game,

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:13.567
let's get comfortable with our workspace.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:16.567
This is Paisley Studio.

00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:20.267
On the left, we have our project area.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:24.267
This is where we see and organise our files.

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:28.433
These three buttons at the top are very useful.

00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:32.033
The first button creates a new file.

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:35.367
The second button creates a new folder.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:38.900
Folders help us keep our work tidy.

00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:41.300
And the third button uploads files,

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:45.600
like pictures, from your computer into your project.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.333
When you choose a file,

00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:50.467
a pencil and a bin appear next to it.

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:54.867
The pencil renames the file, and the bin deletes it.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.967
In the middle is our code editor.

00:00:57.967 --> 00:01:02.033
This is where we write our instructions for the computer.

00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:06.167
And over here, on the right, is our preview.

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:09.900
This is where we see what our work looks like.

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:13.433
Up at the top are two important buttons.

00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:15.367
Save keeps our work safe,

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:19.300
and Run shows our latest changes in the preview.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.167
Let's create our very first file.

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:26.100
Click the new file button.

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:31.100
Type the name index.html, and press Enter.

00:01:31.867 --> 00:01:35.700
There it is, in our project area!

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:40.733
HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.767
It is the language that gives a webpage its structure,

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:47.400
a bit like the frame that holds up a house.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.133
Now for a little coding magic.

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:54.233
Click inside the code editor.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.133
Hold down the Shift key and press the number one.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:01.467
That types an exclamation mark.

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:04.700
Now press Enter.

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:07.067
Wow!

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:11.133
The editor has written a whole webpage starter for us.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:13.067
This shortcut is called Emmet,

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:16.200
and it saves us lots of typing.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.700
Let's look at what each line means.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.867
The <!DOCTYPE html> line tells the browser

00:02:23.867 --> 00:02:26.800
that this is a modern HTML document.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.033
The <html> tag is the big container

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:32.433
that holds our whole webpage.

00:02:32.433 --> 00:02:37.500
lang="en" tells the browser that our page is in English.

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:39.900
Inside, we have the <head>.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.200
The head holds information about our page,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.567
which we don't see on the page itself.

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:49.100
The meta charset line helps the browser

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.467
show letters and symbols correctly.

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:55.300
The viewport line helps our page fit nicely

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:59.000
on phones, tablets and computers.

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:03.433
The title is the name that appears on the browser tab.

00:03:03.733 --> 00:03:06.167
And the <body> holds everything we

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.867
can actually see on the webpage.

00:03:09.233 --> 00:03:11.900
Notice how most tags come in pairs:

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:16.467
an opening tag, and a closing tag with a forward slash.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:20.300
Everything in between belongs to that element.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.467
Let's give our page a proper name.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:29.267
Select the words My page, and type Number Match.

00:03:30.233 --> 00:03:33.167
A meaningful title helps people find our game,

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:36.567
even when they have lots of tabs open.

00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:40.500
Now let's build the structure of our game.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:44.833
We'll go one piece at a time, inside the body.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.267
First, a <main> element.

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:50.533
It holds the main content of our page.

00:03:50.533 --> 00:03:52.667
We give it a class called

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:56.167
app-shell, so we can style it later.

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.567
Next, the <header>.

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:04.300
It holds our brand: a red N, and the words Number Match.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:08.000
Then comes the hero section, with a small line of

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.400
text, a big heading, and a short introduction.

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:15.700
The <h1> tag is our main heading.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.667
Every page should have one.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:25.033
Now the game panel. This is where the game itself lives.

00:04:25.433 --> 00:04:27.967
At the top is a toolbar.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:31.500
It has a select box, so players can choose Easy,

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.533
Medium or Challenge, and a Restart button.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.733
Below that, three stat boxes,

00:04:38.733 --> 00:04:43.167
for the moves, the matched pairs, and the time.

00:04:43.333 --> 00:04:47.367
Each number has an id, like moves or timer.

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:53.000
An id is a unique name, so JavaScript can find it later.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:58.300
Then a progress track, with a progress fill inside it.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:03.500
And here is the most important box of all: the game grid.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.000
It's empty for now, because JavaScript

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.000
will create the cards for us.

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:11.900
Under the grid, a message area,

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:15.033
to tell the player what is happening.

00:05:15.633 --> 00:05:19.167
Then a <footer> at the bottom of the page.

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:22.267
Finally, outside the main element,

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:25.000
we add the celebration screen.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:28.600
It will appear when every pair is matched.

00:05:28.967 --> 00:05:31.133
See how the elements sit inside each

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:34.500
other, like boxes inside boxes?

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.000
That's called nesting.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:42.567
Time to see our work. Click Save.

00:05:42.967 --> 00:05:45.500
Now click Run.

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:48.167
Look at the preview!

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:50.000
Our heading, our stats,

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.467
our buttons and our message are all there.

00:05:53.633 --> 00:05:58.167
It looks very plain right now, and that's completely fine.

00:05:58.167 --> 00:06:02.100
The structure is ready, and that's what matters.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.767
Fantastic work!

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:10.133
You have created the foundation of your very own game.

00:06:10.533 --> 00:06:13.967
But something is missing, isn't it?

00:06:14.167 --> 00:06:19.500
Our game needs colour, personality and beautiful cards.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.267
That's exactly what we are going to

00:06:21.267 --> 00:06:25.067
create in our next lesson with CSS!
